g/2010-annual-report/", "final_url": "https://www.pencom.gov.ng/2010-annual-report/", "text": "Annual Reports Monthly Reports Quarterly Reports Annual Accounts General Publications Pension Reform Act PRA 2014 Resources Downloads PENCOM Seminar & Conferences PENCOM Presentations Speeches Other Related Bodies Site Map Data Protection Data Privacy & Protection Policy Website Privacy Notice ISMS Policy ISMS Policy Document News & Events News Photo Gallery Video Gallery Events Calendar Pension Industry Performance Dashboard Report Employer Pension Contribution Remittance System (PCRS) Contact Us \u00a9 2026 National Pension Commission Annual Reports Home Annual Reports reports 2010 ANNUAL REPORT Download > Publications Annual Reports Annual Accounts FAQS General Publications Monthly Reports Quarterly Reports Related Content 2021 ANNUAL REPORT 2020 ANNUAL REPORT 2019, ANNUAL REPORT 2013 ANNUAL REPORT 2012 ANNUAL REPORT 2011 ANNUAL REPORT Maybeach Technologies Limited 174 Ademola Adetokunbo, Wuse 2, Abuja, Nigeria info@pencom.gov.ng \u00a9 2026 National Pension Commission \u00d7 Cookies We serve cookies. If you think that's ok, just click \"Accept all\". You can also choose what kind of cookies you want by clicking \"Settings\". Read our Privacy Policy Settings Accept all Cookies Choose what kind of cookies to accept. Your choice will be saved for one year. Read our Privacy Policy Necessary These cookies are not optional. They are needed for the website to function. Statistics In order for us to improve the website's functionality and structure, based on how the website is used. Experience In order for our website to perform as well as possible during your visit. If you refuse these cookies, some functionality will disappear from the website. Marketing By sharing your interests and behavior as you visit our site, you increase the chance of seeing personalized content and offers. Save Accept all", "content_hash": "a56d246f5005471f4d3f007be1abf04fa02d3735309db286e3530c500782e421", "domain": "pencom.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:29.118863+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1215", "title": "Annual Reports", "url": "https://www.pencom.gov.ng/2011-annual-report/", "final_url": "https://www.pencom.gov.ng/2011-annual-report/", "text": "Annual Reports Monthly Reports Quarterly Reports Annual Accounts General Publications Pension Reform Act PRA 2014 Resources Downloads PENCOM Seminar & Conferences PENCOM Presentations Speeches Other Related Bodies Site Map Data Protection Data Privacy & Protection Policy Website Privacy Notice ISMS Policy ISMS Policy Document News & Events News Photo Gallery Video Gallery Events Calendar Pension Industry Performance Dashboard Report Employer Pension Contribution Remittance System (PCRS) Contact Us \u00a9 2026 National Pension Commission Annual Reports Home Annual Reports reports 2011 ANNUAL REPORT Download > Publications Annual Reports Annual Accounts FAQS General Publications Monthly Reports Quarterly Reports Related Content 2021 ANNUAL REPORT 2020 ANNUAL REPORT 2019, ANNUAL REPORT 2013 ANNUAL REPORT 2012 ANNUAL REPORT 2011 ANNUAL REPORT Maybeach Technologies Limited 174 Ademola Adetokunbo, Wuse 2, Abuja, Nigeria info@pencom.gov.ng \u00a9 2026 National Pension Commission \u00d7 Cookies We serve cookies. If you think that's ok, just click \"Accept all\". You can also choose what kind of cookies you want by clicking \"Settings\". Read our Privacy Policy Settings Accept all Cookies Choose what kind of cookies to accept. Your choice will be saved for one year. Read our Privacy Policy Necessary These cookies are not optional. They are needed for the website to function. Statistics In order for us to improve the website's functionality and structure, based on how the website is used. Experience In order for our website to perform as well as possible during your visit. If you refuse these cookies, some functionality will disappear from the website. Marketing By sharing your interests and behavior as you visit our site, you increase the chance of seeing personalized content and offers. Save Accept all", "content_hash": "acd818ea99f22c93f5da6001527c391fa51084440b204c4e2fb3bdeae9f602f5", "domain": "pencom.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:30.909479+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1216", "title": "Technology in a  Dangerous World", "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/science-technology-and-society/sts-069-technology-in-a-dangerous-world-fall-2002/index.htm", "final_url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/science-technology-and-society/sts-069-technology-in-a-dangerous-world-fall-2002/index.htm", "text": "Technology in a Dangerous World | Science, Technology, and Society | MIT OpenCourseWare Browse Course Material Syllabus Calendar Readings Assignments Student Anthology Related Resources Study Materials Course Info Instructor Prof. Rosalind Williams Departments Science, Technology, and Society As Taught In Fall 2002 Level Undergraduate Topics Social Science Public Administration Science and Technology Policy Security Studies Sociology Learning Resource Types grading Projects with Examples theaters Workshop Videos assignment Written Assignments Download Course menu search Give Now About OCW Help & Faqs Contact Us search GIVE NOW about ocw help & faqs contact us STS.069 | Fall 2002 | Undergraduate Technology in a Dangerous World Menu Syllabus Calendar Readings Assignments Student Anthology Related Resources Study Materials Course Description Aim is to analyze important current events for what they reveal about the nature and working of our technological world. Starting point is connection between technology and terrorism. Subject also explores how a human-built world can foster insecurity and danger, and how human beings respond. Many invited guests help \u2026Show more Aim is to analyze important current events for what they reveal about the nature and working of our technological world. Starting point is connection between technology and terrorism. Subject also explores how a human-built world can foster insecurity and danger, and how human beings respond. Many invited guests help develop a strong interdisciplinary approach (science, engineering, social science, humanities). Topics include technological risk and remediation, sociotechnical systems, imagination of disaster, technology and identity, technology and religion, technology and education, and technology and trust. Written and oral assignments and a final project required. Service-learning proposals and web-based presentations, in addition to written work, may be considered for the final project by the instructor.Show less Course Info Instructor Prof. Rosalind Williams Departments Science, Technology, and Society Topics Social Science Public Administration Science and Technology Policy Security Studies Sociology Learning Resource Types grading Projects with Examples theaters Workshop Videos assignment Written Assignments Illustration of the rapid decrease in air traffic over the continental United States from 9:00 am to 12:00 pm, September 11, 2001. Each plane in the graphic represents 100 civilian aircraft. (Animation courtesy of Daniel Bersak.) Download Course Over 2,500 courses & materials Freely sharing knowledge with learners and educators around the world. Learn more \u00a9 2001\u20132026 Massachusetts Institute of Technology Accessibility Creative Commons License Terms and Conditions Proud member of: \u00a9 2001\u20132026 Massachusetts Institute of Technology You are leaving MIT OpenCourseWare close Please be advised that external sites may have terms and conditions, including license rights, that differ from ours. MIT OCW is not responsible for any content on third party sites, nor does a link suggest an endorsement of those sites and/or their content. Stay Here Continue", "content_hash": "9feee6408c200cb01455a6e67ba541bcf1ace7ae275784a5060b1a3b0ff1529d", "domain": "ocw.mit.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:31.661463+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1217", "title": "Monthly Reports", "url": "https://www.pencom.gov.ng/2017-february-monthly-report/", "final_url": "https://www.pencom.gov.ng/2017-february-monthly-report/", "text": "Monthly Reports Quarterly Reports Annual Accounts General Publications Pension Reform Act PRA 2014 Resources Downloads PENCOM Seminar & Conferences PENCOM Presentations Speeches Other Related Bodies Site Map Data Protection Data Privacy & Protection Policy Website Privacy Notice ISMS Policy ISMS Policy Document News & Events News Photo Gallery Video Gallery Events Calendar Pension Industry Performance Dashboard Report Employer Pension Contribution Remittance System (PCRS) Contact Us \u00a9 2026 National Pension Commission Monthly Reports Home Monthly Reports Publications 2017 FEBRUARY MONTHLY REPORT Download > SUMMARY OF PENSION FUND ASSETS AS AT 28 FEBRUARY 2017 Publications Monthly Reports Annual Accounts Annual Reports FAQS General Publications Quarterly Reports Related Content Monthly Report \u2013 August 2026 Monthly Report \u2013 July 2026 Monthly Report \u2013 June 2026 PenCom Chronicles Magazine Maybeach Technologies Limited 174 Ademola Adetokunbo, Wuse 2, Abuja, Nigeria info@pencom.gov.ng \u00a9 2026 National Pension Commission \u00d7 Cookies We serve cookies. If you think that's ok, just click \"Accept all\". You can also choose what kind of cookies you want by clicking \"Settings\". Read our Privacy Policy Settings Accept all Cookies Choose what kind of cookies to accept. Your choice will be saved for one year. Read our Privacy Policy Necessary These cookies are not optional. They are needed for the website to function. Statistics In order for us to improve the website's functionality and structure, based on how the website is used. Experience In order for our website to perform as well as possible during your visit. If you refuse these cookies, some functionality will disappear from the website. Marketing By sharing your interests and behavior as you visit our site, you increase the chance of seeing personalized content and offers. Save Accept all", "content_hash": "b16c88d5a659e5c5a72abf0c2e746e5efe746170458bd6c4683d2e2b832bb190", "domain": "pencom.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:32.735852+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1218", "title": "Out of Ground Zero: Catastrophe and Memory", "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/global-languages/21g-013-out-of-ground-zero-catastrophe-and-memory-fall-2005/", "final_url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/global-languages/21g-013-out-of-ground-zero-catastrophe-and-memory-fall-2005/", "text": "Out of Ground Zero: Catastrophe and Memory | Global Studies and Languages | MIT OpenCourseWare Browse Course Material Syllabus Calendar Readings Study Materials Course Info Instructor Prof. Charity Scribner Departments Global Studies and Languages As Taught In Fall 2005 Level Undergraduate Topics Humanities Literature International Literature Social Science Anthropology Cultural Anthropology Sociology Download Course menu search Give Now About OCW Help & Faqs Contact Us search GIVE NOW about ocw help & faqs contact us 21G.013 | Fall 2005 | Undergraduate Out of Ground Zero: Catastrophe and Memory Menu Syllabus Calendar Readings Study Materials Course Description Within twenty-four hours of the attack on the World Trade Center on September 11, 2001 politicians, artists, and cultural critics had begun to ask how to memorialize the deaths of thousands of people. This question persists today, but it can also be countered with another: is building a monument the best way to \u2026Show more Within twenty-four hours of the attack on the World Trade Center on September 11, 2001 politicians, artists, and cultural critics had begun to ask how to memorialize the deaths of thousands of people. This question persists today, but it can also be countered with another: is building a monument the best way to commemorate that moment in history? What might other discourses, media, and art forms offer in such a project of collective memory? How can these cultural formations help us to assess the immediate reaction to the attack? To approach these issues, \u201cOut of Ground Zero\u201d looks back to earlier sites of catastrophe in Germany and Japan.Show less Course Info Instructor Prof. Charity Scribner Departments Global Studies and Languages Topics Humanities Literature International Literature Social Science Anthropology Cultural Anthropology Sociology Beam from the World Trade Center on display in Boston, MA, Sept. 11, 2002. (Image courtesy of Daniel Bersak.) Download Course Over 2,500 courses & materials Freely sharing knowledge with learners and educators around the world. Learn more \u00a9 2001\u20132026 Massachusetts Institute of Technology Accessibility Creative Commons License Terms and Conditions Proud member of: \u00a9 2001\u20132026 Massachusetts Institute of Technology You are leaving MIT OpenCourseWare close Please be advised that external sites may have terms and conditions, including license rights, that differ from ours. MIT OCW is not responsible for any content on third party sites, nor does a link suggest an endorsement of those sites and/or their content. Stay Here Continue", "content_hash": "9ba7279c81d649236ae232b42ebc72d2b6de59cb9414c0f1b9318c25ca500faa", "domain": "ocw.mit.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:33.632255+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1219", "title": "Monthly Reports", "url": "https://www.pencom.gov.ng/2017-january-monthly-report/", "final_url": "https://www.pencom.gov.ng/2017-january-monthly-report/", "text": "Monthly Reports Quarterly Reports Annual Accounts General Publications Pension Reform Act PRA 2014 Resources Downloads PENCOM Seminar & Conferences PENCOM Presentations Speeches Other Related Bodies Site Map Data Protection Data Privacy & Protection Policy Website Privacy Notice ISMS Policy ISMS Policy Document News & Events News Photo Gallery Video Gallery Events Calendar Pension Industry Performance Dashboard Report Employer Pension Contribution R